sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0266 slice 3 proof (D4, D5, D7). docs/reference/executor.md#the-proof-operation.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · Gateway diagnostic and nested proof support
  %% kind: executor.proof
  autonumber
  %% lane RN icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane OB icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane EX icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant RN as Caller<br/>operator / runner
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>nested Gateway
  participant OB as Observer<br/>orbit-agent
  participant EX as Executor<br/>orbit-executor
  RN->>GW: Start a proof on one Node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the runner step `executor_round_trip`, `executor_lost_result` or `executor_publish` runs `tools/swamp-proof-guest/executor-order.php` on the nested Gateway as its managed user
  %%> Who can start it:
  %%> - the diagnostic POST checks the active WireGuard peer, target Node access and Gateway authority
  %%> - the diagnostic requires an empty request body and no query parameters before it records an Operation and sends one order
  Note over GW: Record executor.proof<br/>node_id set · running
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - records a durable Operation on the app-dev Node; its target is the Node (D7)
  %%> Why no Swamp run:
  %%> - `proof.noop` changes nothing on the Node; the Gateway runs and closes the kind itself
  GW->>OB: executor-order<br/>presence-node.{id}
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - signs a `proof.noop` order with a new nonce and publishes it as a server event through Reverb (D5)
  %%> - the data is the Operation id and the order, nothing else
  OB->>EX: Order bytes, unread<br/>/run/orbit-executor.sock
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the observer copies the order unchanged; the executor checks the caller, the signature and the order
  Note over EX: Run proof.noop once<br/>journal open, done
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the no-op under the Node's lock and records it in its journal
  %%> When the Operation already ran:
  %%> - returns the first result as `repeat` and does not act; the journal gets a `seen` record
  EX-->>OB: accepted, then result<br/>two lines
  OB->>GW: client-executor-result<br/>{operation, line}
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the listener checks ownership on both lines, records the result and queues both lines in arrival order for 60 s
  GW->>GW: BLPOP the result<br/>bound ORBIT_EXECUTOR_WAIT_MS
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the waiting request takes the result, as a visit will in slice 6
  opt the nested proof runner tests a lost hand-off
    GW->>OB: New order, same Operation<br/>new nonce
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the executor answers `repeat` with the first result; the listener pushes it again and the waiter gets it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the action ran once; the Operation keeps the first result
  end
  Note over GW: Keep terminal verdict<br/>succeeded, failed or cancelled
  %%> Result:
  %%> - observed `accepted` followed by matching `done` settles an open Operation as `succeeded`
  %%> - when a peer with target Node access cancels first, the Operation stays `cancelled` even if valid replies follow
  %%> - a refusal, timeout or incomplete reply fails an open Operation
  %%> - a signing, publish or wait exception fails an open Operation with `executor.proof_aborted`
  GW-->>RN: Return the verdict
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the diagnostic returns the terminal Operation
  %%> - the proof runner reports each Operation, nonce, result and latency on stdout
